{"nodes": [{"id": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_doc", "label": "Item 15 \u2014 Worker-Only Kernel Invariant in CI", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-02-followup-15-deploy-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Item 13 created a sibling invariant to item 12's and left it enforced by a comment and nothing else. Three edits that would break it all pass CI today. Half of item 15 stays open deliberately: building images in CI would pre-empt item 4's role split, and the check must not decide that design as a side effect."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_check_deploy", "label": "cargo xtask check-deploy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-02-followup-15-deploy-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An xtask subcommand rather than a grep step in ci.yml: a shell grep is three lines but untested, CI-only, and unrunnable locally before a push. Parses deploy/compose.yaml and deploy/Containerfile line-wise \u2014 no serde_yaml, which is unmaintained and would trip cargo deny advisories. The check is static: it verifies the configuration that would produce the right images, never the images."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_worker_only_kernel_invariant", "label": "Worker-Only Kernel Linking Invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-02-followup-15-deploy-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only the worker image links the CAD kernel, because the open path never invokes it. Expressed as a named list of kernel-linked services written generically over all service blocks, so a future api-replica is covered without anyone remembering to add it, plus the requirement that ARG SERVER_FEATURES is declared after the first FROM \u2014 an ARG before it is a different scope and would silently ship a worker with no kernel."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_parse_stale_violation", "label": "Parse-Stale Violation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-02-followup-15-deploy-check.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A line-wise parser that cannot find what it expects must fail loudly, not pass silently \u2014 and its message must say the check's parsing is stale, not that the config is wrong. The two failures need opposite fixes and a check reporting the wrong one sends the reader to the wrong file. Written because a previous round shipped an assertion whose two halves could both degrade to an empty string, compare equal, and pass having verified nothing."}], "edges": [{"source": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_doc", "target": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_check_deploy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-02-followup-15-deploy-check.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_check_deploy", "target": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_worker_only_kernel_invariant", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-02-followup-15-deploy-check.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_parse_stale_violation", "target": "plans_2026_09_02_followup_15_deploy_check_check_deploy", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-02-followup-15-deploy-check.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "